---
import RelationshipExplorer from './RelationshipExplorer.astro';
import {relationshipCards} from '../../lib/studio/relationshipExplorer';
const {project,base,cards=[],families=[],guidebook=[],illustrative=false}=Astro.props;
const moments=['Finding the form','The structure','Card collection','Relationships','Using the system','Deck Blueprint'];
const labels={form:"The deck's form",structure:'Organizing principles',contribution:'The card collection',balance:'Relationships and balance',use:'How the system works',questions:'Open architectural questions'};
---
<section data-chapter-panel="architecture" hidden class="chapter-architecture">
<script type="application/json" id="journey-collection" set:html={JSON.stringify({relationshipCards:relationshipCards(project,cards,families),visualDirection:{colour:project.settings?.visual_direction_v1?.fields?.colour??'',treatment:project.settings?.visual_direction_v1?.fields?.treatment??''},cards:cards.map((c:any)=>({id:c.id,title:c.title,family_id:c.family_id,card_number:c.card_number,correspondences:typeof c.content?.correspondences==='string'?c.content.correspondences:''})),families,guidebook:guidebook.map((s:any)=>({id:s.id,title:s.title,card_id:s.card_id}))}).replaceAll('<','\\u003c')}/>
<nav class="architecture-moments" aria-label="Architecture moments">{moments.map((name,i)=><button type="button" data-document-moment="architecture" data-step={i}>{name}</button>)}</nav>
<section data-document-panel="architecture" data-step="0"><p class="studio-eyebrow">Section three · The Architecture</p><h2>What shape does your idea want to take?</h2><p class="architecture-intro">Some decks follow established systems. Others invent an entirely new way of organizing ideas. Some combine traditions with personal interpretation, while others bring a creative, educational, or professional method into card form.</p><label class="studio-field">The form that could serve my vision<textarea data-architecture-response="form" rows="7"/></label><details><summary>Forms to explore</summary><p>Tarot, oracle, hybrid, professional or educational cards, and original or experimental systems can overlap. Use this reflection to consider a form before changing your project settings or card collection.</p><p>Traditional tarot commonly uses 78 cards; other systems may need a different structure. Choose your guidebook structure separately; you can revise it as your writing develops.</p></details></section>
<section data-document-panel="architecture" data-step="1" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Discovering the structure</p><h2>What holds your deck together?</h2><p>A subject is not the same as an organizing principle. A deck about trees might follow seasons, ecology, symbolism or stages of growth — perhaps several at once.</p><label class="studio-field">The organizing ideas and relationships I already recognize<textarea data-architecture-response="structure" rows="8"/></label><details><summary>Try a way of looking</summary><p>Families or categories · a journey or process · an established framework · an interconnected network · an open collection.</p><p>These are possibilities, not mandatory categories. You can organize your own families when a grouping becomes useful.</p></details></section>
<section data-document-panel="architecture" data-step="2" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The card collection</p><h2>See the deck taking shape.</h2><p>These are your existing cards, shown in another view. Opening one takes you to its current writing; this map does not create a second copy.</p><div class="map-controls"><label class="studio-field">Find a card<input type="search" data-map-search placeholder="Title, number or family"/></label><label class="studio-field">View<select data-map-view><option value="visual">Visual collection</option><option value="list">Editorial list</option></select></label></div><div data-deck-map class="deck-map">{cards.map((c:any,i:number)=><article data-map-card data-card-id={c.id} data-search={`${c.title} ${c.card_number} ${families.find((f:any)=>f.id===c.family_id)?.name??''}`.toLocaleLowerCase()}><button type="button" data-select-card={c.id} aria-label={`Explore ${c.title}`}>{project.settings?.visual_design_v1?.cards?.[c.id]?.front?<img src={project.settings.visual_design_v1.cards[c.id].front} alt={`Artwork for ${c.title}`}/>:<span class="artwork-empty">Add artwork</span>}<span class="map-number">{c.card_number||'Unnumbered'}</span><strong>{c.title}</strong><small>{families.find((f:any)=>f.id===c.family_id)?.name??'No family assigned'}</small></button></article>)}</div>{!cards.length?<p>No cards have been added yet. Begin with one idea in My Workshop; there is no required count.</p>:null}<div data-selected-card class="selected-card" hidden/><label class="studio-field">What does each card contribute that no other card quite addresses?<textarea data-architecture-response="contribution" rows="5"/></label><a href={`${base}/cards/new/`}>Add or develop a card in The Expression</a></section>
<section data-document-panel="architecture" data-step="3" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Relationships and balance</p><h2>What happens between your cards?</h2><p>Complement, contrast, progression, shared imagery, correspondence or deliberate repetition may all matter. Describe the connection in your own words; there is no required taxonomy.</p><RelationshipExplorer base={base}/><div class="connection-compose"><label class="studio-field">One card<select data-connection-from><option value="">Choose a card</option>{cards.map((c:any)=><option value={c.id}>{c.title}</option>)}</select></label><label class="studio-field">Another card<select data-connection-to><option value="">Choose a card</option>{cards.map((c:any)=><option value={c.id}>{c.title}</option>)}</select></label><label class="studio-field">How they connect<input data-connection-kind placeholder="For example: shared symbol, contrast, next stage"/></label><label class="studio-field">Why this matters (optional)<textarea data-connection-note rows="3"/></label><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-add-connection>Add this connection</button><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-cancel-connection hidden>Cancel connection edit</button><p data-connection-status role="status"/></div><div data-connections/><label class="studio-field">Patterns, intentional imbalance or gaps I want to consider<textarea data-architecture-response="balance" rows="6"/></label><p>Similarity is not a mistake. Nothing here merges or deletes cards, or changes existing correspondences.</p></section>
<section data-document-panel="architecture" data-step="4" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Making the system usable</p><h2>Imagine the first use.</h2><p>Drawing one card, exploring a spread, moving through a sequence, browsing a collection or facilitating a conversation: how will someone find their way?</p><label class="studio-field">How the system will work in practice<textarea data-architecture-response="use" rows="8"/></label><details><summary>Questions worth carrying forward</summary><p>Can a card stand alone? Does order matter? What will the companion need to explain? Compare these choices with your Creative Brief without treating a tension as an automatic error.</p><label class="studio-field">Open architectural questions<textarea data-architecture-response="questions" rows="5"/></label></details></section>
<section data-document-panel="architecture" data-step="5" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">A working map, not a final set of rules</p><h2>My Deck Blueprint</h2><p>Keep your structural thinking beside the actual collection. Bringing your words here does not alter cards, families or their order.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-assemble="architecture">Bring my words into the blueprint</button>{Object.entries(labels).map(([key,label])=><label class="studio-field">{label}<textarea data-architecture-output={key} rows="4" placeholder=""/></label>)}<details><summary>Original architecture reflections</summary><div data-original-document="architecture"/></details><details><summary>Earlier saved blueprints</summary><div data-document-history="architecture"/></details><p>Your deck is becoming a system. Your Blueprint can evolve as the cards reveal more of the story.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-chapter="expression">Explore The Expression</button><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-document-moment="architecture" data-step="2">Open my Deck Map</button></section>
<div class="architecture-actions"><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-save-document>Save my Architecture</button><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-document-next="architecture">Continue</button></div><a href={`${base}/`}>Open My Workshop at any time</a>
</section>
<style>.chapter-architecture h2{font:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem)/1.2 'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif}.chapter-architecture p{line-height:1.75}.architecture-intro{font-size:1.14rem}.architecture-moments{display:flex;gap:.35rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:1.8rem}.architecture-moments button{background:none;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;padding:.5rem .35rem;font:inherit;color:inherit}.architecture-moments button[aria-current]{border-color:#526f7b;font-weight:700}.chapter-architecture .studio-field{display:grid;gap:.55rem;margin:1.2rem 0;font-weight:600}.chapter-architecture textarea,.chapter-architecture input,.chapter-architecture select{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:400 1rem/1.6 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;padding:.8rem;background:white;border:1px solid #9d9e94;border-radius:4px;color:#242b2b}.chapter-architecture textarea{resize:vertical}.chapter-architecture details{border-top:1px solid #cec9c1;padding:1rem 0}.chapter-architecture summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}.map-controls{display:flex;gap:1rem}.map-controls .studio-field{flex:1;min-width:0}.deck-map{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.deck-map article{min-width:0}.deck-map button{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.4rem;width:100%;padding:.6rem;border:1px solid #cec9c1;background:#fff;color:inherit;font:inherit;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}.deck-map svg{width:100%;max-height:160px}.deck-map .map-number{font-size:.75rem}.deck-map small{font-size:.8rem}.deck-map[data-view=list]{grid-template-columns:1fr}.deck-map[data-view=list] svg{display:none}.map-illustration-note{font-size:.8rem;color:#58605d}.selected-card,.connection-compose{padding:1rem;background:#e6eceb;margin:1rem 0}.architecture-actions{display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:2rem 0 1rem}.chapter-architecture [data-original-document] p,.chapter-architecture [data-document-history] p{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.chapter-architecture button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #065e73;outline-offset:3px}.chapter-architecture :global(.connection-item){border-bottom:1px solid #cec9c1;padding:1rem 0}.chapter-architecture :global(.connection-item button){margin:.6rem 0}.chapter-architecture :global(.connection-item p){white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){.deck-map{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.map-controls{display:block}.architecture-actions .studio-button{width:100%}}</style>

<style>.architecture-moments{margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:.83rem;gap:.2rem}.deck-map{gap:.8rem}.deck-map button{padding:.5rem;background:#fbf9f4;border-radius:4px;transition:border-color .15s}.deck-map button:hover{border-color:#8a6a1f}.map-study{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:5/7;object-fit:cover;border-radius:2px}.deck-map strong{font:1.12rem/1.2 'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif}.deck-map[data-view=list] .map-study{display:none}.deck-map[data-view=list] button{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr;align-items:center}.deck-map[data-view=list] small{grid-column:2}</style>